  "answers": {
    "q1_split_property_sources": "Successful representations are most associated with: purity gain is weakly associated with macro F1 (spearman=0.035); boundary-preserving splits (log-boundary \u0394 spearman=-0.179, parent log-boundary spearman=0.229); more splits correlate with worse outcomes (n_splits spearman=-0.581). Parent boundary structure (log-boundary) is the strongest positive signal; purity gain alone is insufficient and over-splitting hurts.",
    "q2_why_rho90": "rho=0.90 achieves mean macro F1 0.597 (B0=0.569, rho=0.95=0.569, \u0394 vs B0=+0.0274). It proposes 239.7 splits vs B0 267.7, with mean log-boundary change -0.4855 and mean radius change 87.0386. Stopping at \u03c1=0.90 retains boundary-rich mixed balls while avoiding the over-fragmentation and excessive heterogeneity of \u03c1=0.95 / B0.",
    "q3_why_su3_fails": "SU3 mean macro F1 0.556 vs B0 0.569 (\u0394=-0.0201). SU3 rejects 26.1 splits/run (acceptance 51.2%), producing fewer balls (41.9 vs B0 88.8) with lower purity gain (\u0394=-0.0640) and different boundary structure (\u0394 log-boundary=+0.1431). The SU3 gate filters on compactness/separation utility, not boundary score \u2014 it removes splits that would refine boundary structure while retaining heterogeneous coarse balls. Fewer, larger balls with suppressed boundary refinement hurt Gaussian-weighted twin-hyperplane geometry. Rejected splits have lower log-boundary change (-0.1810) than accepted (-0.3104).",
    "q4_future_objective": "A future split objective should optimize boundary structure over purity: parent log-boundary (spearman=0.229) correlates positively with macro F1, while more splits (spearman=-0.581) correlate negatively. Combine: (1) preserve or increase log-boundary score (entropy \u00d7 density), (2) moderate compactness gain without over-fragmentation, (3) protect minority survival (mean_min_surv_change spearman=0.559), (4) stop recursion near \u03c1\u22480.90 rather than pursuing \u03c1\u21921. Reject splits that reduce boundary structure or create del_ball-vulnerable minority peels."
  }
}